# oracle: compute born/matrix numdiff evaluates its 12 strained configurations on the step's neighbor list, as native
#   LAMMPS does (src/EXTRA-COMPUTE/compute_born_matrix.cpp compute_numdiff at b332f28: displace_atoms of the owned and
#   ghost atoms in the unchanged box, then update_virial); with neighbor skin 0 a rebuilt list adds or drops the pairs
#   that the strain carries across the cutoff, and their force jump over 2 delta enters the Born terms. The running
#   averages of fix ave/time over c_born (examples/ELASTIC_T/BORN_MATRIX/Argon/Numdiff, shortened) show it.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-7 abs=1e-8
units           real
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 5.405
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 39.948
velocity        all create 60.0 87287 loop geom
velocity        all zero linear
pair_style      lj/cut 9.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.238067 3.405
neighbor        0.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check no
timestep        2.0
compute         VIR all pressure NULL virial
compute         born all born/matrix numdiff 1e-6 VIR
fix             CB all ave/time 1 50 50 c_born[*] ave running
fix             1 all nvt temp 60.0 60.0 100
thermo_style    custom step temp press c_born[1] f_CB[1] c_born[4] f_CB[4] f_CB[7] f_CB[12] f_CB[21]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             300
